:: R3_TheHallway [r3 story]
<<location "Floor 42, Corridor">>
<<objective "Get back down to Floor 39.">>

The corridor is still empty. 7:14 AM. The building is waking up below me. I can hear the elevator ding on a lower floor, the distant murmur of the lobby. Up here, nothing. Just my footsteps on carpet that absorbs sound like a confession booth.

My hand is in my jacket pocket. Fingers touching the silk through the lining. I pull my hand out. Put it back. Pull it out again. A nervous habit I'm developing in real time, like watching myself grow a new limb.

<<moodimage "files/images/mood/jacket_pocket.png" "">>

<<scene "Elevator, Descending" "files/images/locations/elevator_r3.png">>

The elevator arrives. I step in. The doors close and I'm alone with my reflection in the polished steel. Same face. Same tie. Same shoes with the scuff on the left toe. Same Daniel Ashford who walked into this building ninety minutes ago.

Not the same. Something moved. Something small and interior, like furniture being rearranged in a room I thought was empty.

I press the button for 39. My floor. My lane. My adequate, dependable, unremarkable lane.

<<moodimage "files/images/mood/elevator_numbers.png" "">>

The silk shifts in my pocket as the elevator descends.

<div class="continue-wrap">
    <<link "Continue" "R3_HarperHallway">><</link>>
</div>

:: R3_HarperHallway [r3 story]
<<location "Elevator Bank, Floor 39">>
<<portrait "files/images/characters/harper_casual_r3.png" "Harper Quinn">>
<<objective "Get through the rest of the day.">>

Harper is by the elevator bank when the doors open. She's got a coffee in one hand and a folder in the other and her hair is up in that efficient twist she does when she's already working before she's technically at work.

<<say "Harper Quinn">>Early meeting with Cross?<</say>>

She falls into step beside me. Her eyes do that thing. The cataloguing thing. She takes in my face the way an auditor takes in a spreadsheet. Line by line. Looking for the number that doesn't add up.

<<say "Harper Quinn">>How'd it go?<</say>>

<<sayself>>Fine.<</sayself>>

The word comes out too fast. A bullet exiting a chamber. Fine. The universal shield. The word men use when they have no intention of telling you a single goddamn thing.

Harper tilts her head. The motion is small. Precise. I've worked with her for eight months and I've learned that head tilt. It means she's filing something for later. Not pushing now. But not forgetting.

<<say "Harper Quinn">>Coffee's fresh if you want some.<</say>>

She gestures toward the kitchenette with her folder.

<<sayself>>Thanks.<</sayself>>

I walk past her. My hand goes to the pocket again. Fingers press against the silk through the fabric of my jacket. A phantom touch. A secret handshake with a new version of myself I haven't met yet.

Harper watches me go. I can feel her eyes on my back like a hand between my shoulder blades. She's seen something. She doesn't know what she's seen. Neither do I.

<div class="continue-wrap">
    <<link "Continue" "R3_Afternoon_Hub">><</link>>
</div>

:: R3_Afternoon_Hub [r3 hub]
<<location "Meridian Consulting, Floor 39">>
<<objective "Get through the rest of the day.">>

The morning settles into its ordinary shape around me. Emails. A team call. The building doesn't know what happened on Floor 42, and I'm not sure I do either.

<div class="choice-container">
    <<if !$flags.r3HarperLunch>>
        <span class="sidequest"><<link "Grab lunch with Harper" "R3_SQ_HarperLunch">><</link>></span>
